Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	1	An eunuch, whose testicles are broken or cut away, or yard cut off, shall not enter into the church of the Lord.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	2	A mamzer, that is to say, one born of a prostitute, shall not enter into the church of the Lord, until the tenth generation.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	3	The Ammonite and the Moabite, even after the tenth generation shall not enter into the church of the Lord for ever:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	4	Because they would not meet you with bread and water in the way, when you came out of Egypt: and because they hired against thee Balaam, the son of Beer, from Mesopotamia in Syria, to curse thee.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	5	And the Lord thy God would not hear Balaam, and he turned his cursing into thy blessing, because he loved thee.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	6	Thou shalt not make peace with them, neither shalt thou seek their prosperity all the days of thy life for ever.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	7	Thou shalt not abhor the Edomite, because he is thy brother: nor the Egyptian, because thou wast a stranger in his land.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	8	They that are born of them, in the third generation shall enter into the church of the Lord.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	9	When thou goest out to war against thy enemies, thou shalt keep thyself from every evil thing.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	10	If there be among you any man, that is defiled in a dream by night, he shall go forth out of the camp.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	11	And shall not return, before he be washed with water in the evening: and after sunset he shall return into the camp.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	12	Thou shalt have a place without the camp, to which thou mayst go for the necessities of nature,
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	13	Carrying a paddle at thy girdle. And when thou sittest down, thou shalt dig round about, and with the earth that is dug up thou shalt cover
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	14	That which thou art eased of: (for the Lord thy God walketh in the midst of thy camp, to deliver thee, and to give up thy enemies to thee:) and let thy camp be holy, and let no uncleanness appear therein, lest he go away from thee.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	15	Thou shalt not deliver to his master the servant that is fled to thee.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	16	He shall dwell with thee in the place that shall please him, and shall rest, in one of thy cities: give him no trouble.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	17	There shall be no whore among the daughters of Israel, nor whoremonger among the sons of Israel.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	18	Thou shalt not offer the hire of a strumpet, nor the price of a dog, in the house of the Lord thy God, whatsoever it be that thou hast vowed: because both these are an abomination to the Lord thy God.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	19	Thou shalt not lend to thy brother money to usury, nor corn, nor any other thing:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	20	But to the stranger. To thy brother thou shalt lend that which he wanteth, without usury: that the Lord thy God may bless thee in all thy works in the land, which thou shalt go in to possess.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	21	When thou hast made a vow to the Lord thy God, thou shalt not delay to pay it: because the Lord thy God will require it. And if thou delay, it shall be imputed to thee for a sin.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	22	If thou wilt not promise, thou shalt be without sin.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	23	But that which is once gone out of thy lips, thou shalt observe, and shalt do as thou hast promised to the Lord thy God, and hast spoken with thy own will and with thy own mouth.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	24	Going into thy neighbour's vineyard, thou mayst eat as many grapes as thou pleasest: but must carry none out with thee:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	23	25	If thou go into thy friend's corn, thou mayst break the ears, and rub them in thy hand: but not reap them with a sickle.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	1	If a man take a wife, and have her, and she find not favour in his eyes, for some uncleanness: he shall write a bill of divorce, and shall give it in her hand, and send her out of his house.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	2	And when she is departed, and marrieth another husband,
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	3	And he also hateth her, and hath given her a bill of divorce, and hath sent her out of his house or is dead:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	4	The former husband cannot take her again to wife: because she is defiled, and is become abominable before the Lord: lest thou cause thy land to sin, which the Lord thy God shall give thee to possess.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	5	When a man hath lately taken a wife, he shall not go out to war, neither shall any public business be enjoined him, but he shall be free at home without fault, that for one year he may rejoice with his wife.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	6	Thou shalt not take the nether, nor the upper millstone to pledge: for he hath pledged his life to thee.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	7	If any man be found soliciting his brother of the children of Israel, and selling him shall take a price, he shall be put to death, and thou shalt take away the evil from the midst of thee.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	8	Observe diligently that thou incur not the stroke of the leprosy, but thou shalt do whatsoever the priests of the Levitical race shall teach thee, according to what I have commanded them, and fulfill thou it carefully.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	9	Remember what the Lord your God did to Mary, in the way when you came out of Egypt.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	10	When thou shalt demand of thy neighbour any thing that he oweth thee, thou shalt not go into his house to take away a pledge:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	11	But then shalt stand without, and he shall bring out to thee what he hath.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	12	But if he be poor, the pledge shall not lodge with thee that night,
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	13	But thou shalt restore it to him presently before the going down of the sun: that he may sleep in his own raiment and bless thee, and thou mayst have justice before the Lord thy God.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	14	Thou shalt not refuse the hire of the needy, and the poor, whether he be thy brother, or a stranger that dwelleth with thee in the land, and is within thy gates:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	15	But thou shalt pay him the price of his labour the same day, before the going down of the sun, because he is poor, and with it maintaineth his life: lest he cry against thee to the Lord, and it be reputed to thee for a sin.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	16	The fathers shall not be put to death for the children, nor the children for the fathers, but every one shall die for his own sin.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	17	Thou shalt not pervert the judgment of the stranger nor of the fatherless, neither shalt thou take away the widow's raiment for a pledge.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	18	Remember that thou wast a slave in Egypt, and the Lord thy God delivered thee from thence. Therefore I command thee to do this thing.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	19	When thou hast reaped the corn in thy field, and hast forgot and left a sheaf, thou shalt not return to take it away: but thou shalt suffer the stranger, and the fatherless and the widow to take it away: that the Lord thy God may bless thee in all the works of thy hands.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	20	If thou have gathered the fruit of thy olive trees, thou shalt not return to gather whatsoever remaineth on the trees: but shalt leave it for the stranger, for the fatherless, and the widow.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	21	If thou make the vintage of thy vineyard, thou shalt not gather the clusters that remain, but they shall be for the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	24	22	Remember that thou also wast a bondman in Egypt, and therefore I command thee to do this thing.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	1	If there be a controversy between men, and they call upon the judges: they shall give the prize of justice to him whom they perceive to be just: and him whom they find to be wicked, they shall condemn of wickedness.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	2	And if they see that the offender be worthy of stripes: they shall lay him down, and shall cause him to be beaten before them. According to the measure of the sin shall the measure also of the stripes be:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	3	Yet so, that they exceed not the number of forty: lest thy brother depart shamefully torn before thy eyes.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	4	Thou shalt not muzzle the ox that treadeth out thy corn on the floor.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	5	When brethren dwell together, and one of them dieth without children, the wife of the deceased shall not marry to another: but his brother shall take her, and raise up seed for his brother:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	6	And the first son he shall have of her he shall call by his name, that his name be not abolished out of Israel.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	7	But if he will not take his brother's wife, who by law belongeth to him, the woman shall go to the gate of the city, and call upon the ancients, and say: My husband's brother refuseth to raise up his brother's name in Israel: and will not take me to wife.
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	8	And they shall cause him to be sent for forthwith, and shall ask him. If he answer: I will not take her to wife:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	9	The woman shall come to him before the ancients, and shall take off his shoe from his foot, and spit in his face, and say: So shall it be done to the man that will not build up his brother's house:
Deuteronomy	Dt	5	25	10	And his name shall be called in Israel, the house of the unshod.
