1 Kings	1Ki	9	26	21	And Saul said: I have sinned, return, my son David, for I will no more do thee harm, because my life hath been precious in thy eyes this day: for it appeareth that I have done foolishly, and have been ignorant in very many things.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	26	22	And David answering, said: Behold the king's spear: let one of the king's servants come over and fetch it.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	26	23	And the Lord will reward every one according to his justice, and his faithfulness: for the Lord hath delivered thee this day into my hand, and I would not put forth my hand against the Lord's anointed.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	26	24	And as thy life hath been much set by this day in my eyes, so let my life be much set by in the eyes of the Lord, and let him deliver me from all distress.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	26	25	Then Saul said to David: Blessed art thou, my son David: and truly doing thou shalt do, and prevailing thou shalt prevail. And David went on his way, and Saul returned to his place.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	1	And David said in his heart: I shall one day or other fall into the hands of Saul: is it not better for me to flee, and to be saved in the land of the Philistines, that Saul may despair of me, and cease to seek me in all the coasts of Israel? I will flee then out of his hands.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	2	And David arose and went away, both he and the six hundred men that were with him, to Achis the son of Maoch, king of Geth.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	3	And David dwelt with Achis at Geth, he and his men: every man with his household, and David with his two wives, Achinoam the Jezrahelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal of Carmel.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	4	And it was told Saul that David was fled to Geth, and he sought no more after him.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	5	And David said to Achis: If I have found favour in thy sight, let a place be given me in one of the cities of this country, that I may dwell there: for why should thy servant dwell in the royal city with thee?
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	6	Then Achis gave him Siceleg that day: for which reason Siceleg belongeth to the kings of Juda unto this day.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	7	And the time that David dwelt in the country of the Philistines, was four months.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	8	And David and his men went up, and pillaged Gessuri, and Gerzi, and the Amalecites: for these were of old the inhabitants of the countries, as men go to Sur, even to the land of Egypt.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	9	And David wasted all the land, and left neither man nor woman alive: and took away the sheep and the oxen, and the asses, and the camels, and the apparel, and returned and came to Achis.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	10	And Achis said to him: Whom hast thou gone against today? David answered: Against the south of Juda, and against the south of Jerameel, and against the south of Ceni.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	11	And David saved neither man nor woman, neither brought he any of them to Geth, saying: Lest they should speak against us. So did David, and such was his proceeding all the days that he dwelt in the country of the Philistines.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	27	12	And Achis believed David, saying: He hath done much harm to his people Israel: therefore he shall be my servant for ever.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	1	And it came to pass in those days, that the Philistines gathered together their armies to be prepared for war against Israel: and Achis said to David: Know thou now assuredly, that thou shalt go out with me to the war, thou, and thy men.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	2	And David said to Achis: Now thou shalt know what thy servant will do. And Achis said to David: And I will appoint thee to guard my life for ever.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	3	Now Samuel was dead, and all Israel mourned for him, and buried him in Ramatha his city. And Saul had put away all the magicians and soothsayers out of the land.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	4	And the Philistines were gathered together, and came and camped in Sunam: and Saul also gathered together all Israel, and came to Gelboe.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	5	And Saul saw the army of the Philistines, and was afraid, and his heart was very much dismayed.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	6	And he consulted the Lord, and he answered him not, neither by dreams, nor by priests, nor by prophets.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	7	And Saul said to his servants: Seek me a woman that hath a divining spirit, and I will go to her, and inquire by her. And his servants said to him: There is a woman that hath a divining spirit at Endor.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	8	Then he disguised himself: and put on other clothes, and he went, and two men with him, and they came to the woman by night, and he said to her: Divine to me by thy divining spirit, and bring me up him whom I shall tell thee.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	9	And the woman said to him: Behold thou knowest all that Saul hath done, and how he hath rooted out the magicians and soothsayers from the land: why then dost thou lay a snare for my life, to cause me to be put to death?
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	10	And Saul swore unto her by the Lord, saying: As the Lord liveth there shall no evil happen to thee for this thing.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	11	And the woman said to him: Whom shall I bring up to thee? And he said, Bring me up Samuel.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	12	And when the woman saw Samuel, she cried out with a loud voice, and said to Saul: Why hast thou deceived me? for thou art Saul.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	13	And the king said to her: Fear not: what hast thou seen? And the woman said to Saul: I saw gods ascending out of the earth.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	14	And he said to her: What form is he of? And she said: An old man cometh up, and he is covered with a mantle. And Saul understood that it was Samuel, and he bowed himself with his face to the ground, and adored.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	15	And Samuel said to Saul: Why hast thou disturbed my rest, that I should be brought up? And Saul said, I am in great distress: for the Philistines fight against me, and God is departed from me, and would not hear me, neither by the hand of prophets, nor by dreams: therefore I have called thee, that thou mayest shew me what I shall do.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	16	And Samuel said: Why askest thou me, seeing the Lord has departed from thee, and is gone over to thy rival:
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	17	For the Lord will do to thee as he spoke by me, and he will rend thy kingdom out of thy hand, and will give it to thy neighbour David:
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	18	Because thou didst not obey the voice of the Lord, neither didst thou execute the wrath of his indignation upon Amalec. Therefore hath the Lord done to thee what thou sufferest this day.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	19	And the Lord also will deliver Israel with thee into the hands of the Philistines: and tomorrow thou and thy sons shall be with me: and the Lord will also deliver the army of Israel into the hands of the Philistines.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	20	And forthwith Saul fell all along on the ground, for he was frightened with the words of Samuel, and there was no strength in him, for he had eaten no bread all that day.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	21	And the woman came to Saul (for he was very much troubled) and said to him: Behold thy handmaid hath obeyed thy voice, and I have put my life in my hand: and I hearkened unto the words which thou spokest to me.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	22	Now therefore hear thou also the voice of thy handmaid, and let me set before thee a morsel of bread, that thou mayest eat and recover strength, and be able to go on thy journey.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	23	But he refused, and said: I will not eat. But his servants and the woman forced him, and at length hearkening to their voice, he arose from the ground and sat upon the bed.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	24	Now the woman had a fatted calf in the house, and she made haste and killed it: and taking meal kneaded it, and baked some unleavened bread,
1 Kings	1Ki	9	28	25	And set it before Saul, and before his servants. And when they had eaten they rose up, and walked all that night.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	1	Now all the troops of the Philistines were gathered together to Aphec: and Israel also camped by the fountain which is in Jezrahel.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	2	And the lords of the Philistines marched with their hundreds and their thousands: but David and his men were in the rear with Achis.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	3	And the princes of the Philistines said to Achis: What mean these Hebrews? And Achis said to the princes of the Philistines: Do you not know David, who was the servant of Saul the king of Israel, and hath been with me many days, or years, and I have found no fault in him, since the day that he fled over to me until this day?
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	4	But the princes of the Philistines were angry with him, and they said to him: Let this man return, and abide in his place, which thou hast appointed him, and let him not go down with us to battle, lest he be an adversary to us, when we shall begin to fight: for how can he otherwise appease his master, but with our heads?
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	5	Is not this David, to whom they sung in their dances, saying: Saul slew his thousands, and David his ten thousands?
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	6	Then Achis called David, and said to him: As the Lord liveth, thou art upright and good in my sight: and so is thy going out, and thy coming in with me in the army: and I have not found my evil in thee, since the day that thou camest to me unto this day: but thou pleasest not the lords.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	7	Return therefore, and go in peace, and offend not the eyes of the princes of the Philistines.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	8	And David said to Achis: But what have I done, and what hast thou found in me thy servant, from the day that I have been in thy sight until this day, that I may not go and fight against the enemies of my lord the king?
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	9	And Achis answering said to David: I know that thou art good in my sight, as an angel of God: but the princes of the Philistines have said: He shall not go up with us to the battle.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	10	Therefore arise in the morning, thou, and the servants of thy lord, who came with thee: and when you are up before day, and it shall begin to be light, go on your way.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	29	11	So David and his men arose in the night, that they might set forward in the morning, and returned to the land of the Philistines: and the Philistines went up to Jezrahel.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	1	Now when David and his men were come to Siceleg on the third day, the Amalecites had made an invasion on the south side upon Siceleg, and had smitten Siceleg, and burnt it with fire.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	2	And had taken the women captives that were in it, both little and great: and they had not killed any person, but had carried them with them, and went on their way.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	3	So when David and his men came to the city, and found it burnt with fire, and that their wives and their sons, and their daughters were taken captives,
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	4	David and the people that were with him, lifted up their voices, and wept till they had no more tears.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	5	For the two wives also of David were taken captives, Achinoam the Jezrahelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal of Carmel.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	6	And David was greatly afflicted: for the people had a mind to stone him, for the soul of every man was bitterly grieved for his sons, and daughters: but David took courage in the Lord his God.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	7	And he said to Abiathar the priest the son of Achimelech: Bring me hither the ephod. And Abiathar brought the ephod to David.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	8	And David consulted the Lord, saying: Shall I pursue after these robbers, and shall I overtake them, or not? And the Lord said to him: Pursue after them: for thou shalt surely overtake them and recover the prey.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	9	So David went, he and the six hundred men that were with him, and they came to the torrent Besor: and some being weary stayed there.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	10	But David pursued, he and four hundred men: for two hundred stayed, who being weary could not go over the torrent Besor.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	11	And they found an Egyptian in the field, and brought him to David: and they gave him bread to eat, and water to drink,
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	12	As also a piece of a cake of figs, and two bunches of raisins. And when he had eaten them his spirit returned, and he was refreshed: for he had not eaten bread, nor drunk water three days, and three nights.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	13	And David said to him: To whom dost thou belong? or whence dost thou come? and whither art thou going? He said: I am a young man of Egypt, the servant of an Amalecite, and my master left me, because I began to be sick three days ago.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	14	For we made an invasion on the south side of Cerethi, and upon Juda, and upon the south of Caleb, and we burnt Siceleg with fire.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	15	And David said to him: Canst thou bring me to this company? And he said: Swear to me by God, that thou wilt not kill me, nor deliver me into the hands of my master, and I will bring thee to this company. And David swore to him.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	16	And when he had brought him, behold they were lying spread upon all the ground, eating and drinking, and as it were keeping a festival day, for all the prey, and the spoils which they had taken out of the land of the Philistines, and out of the land of Juda.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	17	And David slew them from the evening unto the evening of the next day, and there escaped not a man of them, but four hundred young men, who had gotten upon camels, and fled.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	18	So David recovered all that the Amalecites had taken, and he rescued his two wives.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	19	And there was nothing missing small or great, neither of their sons or their daughters, nor of the spoils, and whatsoever they had taken: David recovered all.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	20	And he took all the flocks and the herds, and made them go before him: and they said: This is the prey of David.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	21	And David came to the two hundred men, who being weary had stayed, and were not able to follow David, and he had ordered them to abide at the torrent Besor: and they came out to meet David, and the people that were with him. And David coming to the people saluted them peaceably.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	22	Then all the wicked and unjust men that had gone with David answering, said: Because they came not with us, we will not give them any thing of the prey which we have recovered: but let every man take his wife and his children, and be contented with them, and go his way.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	23	But David said: You shall not do so, my brethren, with these things, which the Lord hath given us, who hath kept us, and hath delivered the robbers that invaded us into our hands.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	24	And no man shall hearken to you in this matter. But equal shall be the portion of him that went down to battle and of him that abode at the baggage, and they shall divide alike.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	25	And this hath been done from that day forward, and since was made a statute, and an ordinance, and as a law in Israel.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	26	Then David came to Siceleg, and sent presents of the prey to the ancients of Juda his neighbours, saying: Receive a blessing of the prey of the enemies of the Lord.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	27	To them that were in Bethel, and that were in Ramoth to the south, and to them that were in Jether,
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	28	And to them that were in Aroer and that were in Sephamoth, and that were in Esthamo,
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	29	And that were in Rachal, and that were in the cities of Jerameel, and that were in the cities of Ceni,
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	30	And that were in Arama, and that were in the lake Asan, and that were in Athach,
1 Kings	1Ki	9	30	31	And that were in Hebron, and to the rest that were in those places, in which David had abode with his men.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	1	And the Philistines fought against Israel, and the men of Israel fled from before the Philistines, and fell down slain in mount Gelboe.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	2	And the Philistines fell upon Saul, and upon his sons, and they slew Jonathan, and Abinadab and Melchisua the sons of Saul.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	3	And the whole weight of the battle was turned upon Saul: and the archers overtook him, and he was grievously wounded by the archers.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	4	Then Saul said to his armourbearer: Draw thy sword, and kill me: lest these uncircumcised come, and slay me, and mock at me. And his armourbearer would not: for he was struck with exceeding great fear. Then Saul took his sword, and fell upon it.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	5	And when his armourbearer saw this, to wit, that Saul was dead, he also fell upon his sword and died with him.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	6	So Saul died, and his three sons, and his armourbearer, and all his men that same day together.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	7	And the men of Israel, that were beyond the valley, and beyond the Jordan, seeing that the Israelites were fled, and that Saul was dead, and his sons, forsook their cities, and fled: and the Philistines came, and dwelt there.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	8	And on the morrow the Philistines came to strip the slain, and they found Saul and his three sons lying in mount Gelboe.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	9	And they cut off Saul's head, and stripped him of his armour, and sent into the land of the Philistines round about, to publish it in the temples of their idols, and among their people.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	10	And they put his armour in the temple of Astaroth, but his body they hung on the wall of Bethsan.
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	11	Now when the inhabitants of Jabes Galaad had heard all that the Philistines had done to Saul,
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	12	All the most valiant men arose, and walked all the night, and took the body of Saul, and the bodies of his sons, from the wall of Bethsan: and they came to Jabes Galaad, and burnt them there:
1 Kings	1Ki	9	31	13	And they took their bones and buried them in the wood of Jabes: and fasted seven days.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	1	Now it came to pass, after Saul was dead, that David returned from the slaughter of the Amalecites, and abode two days in Siceleg.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	2	And on the third day, there appeared a man who came out of Saul's camp, with his garments rent, and dust strewed on his head: and when he came to David, he fell upon his face, and adored.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	3	And David said to him: From whence comest thou? And he said to him: I am fled out of the camp of Israel.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	4	And David said unto him: What is the matter that is come to pass? tell me. He said: The people are fled from the battle, and many of the people are fallen and dead: moreover Saul and Jonathan his son are slain.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	5	And David said to the young man that told him: How knowest thou that Saul and Jonathan his son, are dead?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	6	And the young man that told him, said: I came by chance upon mount Gelboe, and Saul leaned upon his spear: and the chariots and horsemen drew nigh unto him,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	7	And looking behind him, and seeing me, he called me. And I answered, Here am I.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	8	And he said to me: Who art thou? And I said to him: I am an Amalecite.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	9	And he said to me: Stand over me, and kill me: for anguish is come upon me, and as yet my whole life is in me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	10	So standing over him, I killed him: for I knew that he could not live after the fall: and I took the diadem that was on his head, and the bracelet that was on his arm and have brought them hither to thee, my lord.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	11	Then David took hold of his garments and rent them, and likewise all the men that were with him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	12	And they mourned, and wept, and fasted until evening for Saul, and for Jonathan his son, and for the people of the Lord, and for the house of Israel, because they were fallen by the sword.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	13	And David said to the young man that told him: Whence art thou? He answered: I am the son of a stranger of Amalee.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	14	David said to him: Why didst thou not fear to put out thy hand to kill the Lord's anointed?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	15	And David calling one of his servants, said: Go near and fall upon him. And he struck him so that he died.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	16	And David said to him: Thy blood be upon thy own head: for thy own mouth hath spoken against thee, saying: I have slain the Lord's anointed.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	17	And David made this kind of lamentation over Saul, and over Jonathan his son.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	18	(Also he commanded that they should teach the children of Juda the use of the bow, as it is written in the book of the just.) And he said: Consider, O Israel, for them that are dead, wounded on thy high places.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	19	The illustrious of Israel are slain upon thy mountains: how are the valiant fallen?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	20	Tell it not in Geth, publish it not in the streets of Ascalon: lest the daughters of the Philistines rejoice, lest the daughters of the uncircumcised triumph,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	21	Ye mountains of Gelboe, let neither dew, nor rain come upon you, neither be they fields of firstfruits: for there was cast away the shield of the valiant, the shield of Saul as though he had not been anointed with oil.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	22	From the blood of the slain, from the fat of the valiant, the arrow of Jonathan never turned back, and the sword of Saul did not return empty.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	23	Saul and Jonathan, lovely, and comely in their life, even in death they were not divided: they were swifter than eagles, stronger than lions.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	24	Ye daughters of Israel, weep over Saul, who clothed you with scarlet in delights, who gave ornaments of gold for your attire.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	25	How are the valiant fallen in battle? Jonathan slain in the high places?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	26	I grieve for thee, my brother Jonathan: exceeding beautiful, and amiable to me above the love of women. As the mother loveth her only son, so did I love thee.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	1	27	How are the valiant fallen, and the weapons of war perished?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	1	And after these things David consulted the Lord, saying: Shall I go up into one of the cities of Juda? And the Lord said to him: Go up. And David said: Whither shall I go up? And he answered him: Into Hebron.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	2	So David went up, and his two wives, Achinoam the Jezrahelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal of Carmel:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	3	And the men also that were with him, David brought up every man with his household: and they abode in the towns of Hebron.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	4	And the men of Juda came, and anointed David there, to be king over the house of Juda. And it was told David, that the men of Jabes Galaad had buried Saul.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	5	David therefore sent messengers to the men of Jabes Galaad, and said to them: Blessed be you to the Lord, who have shewn this mercy to your master Saul, and have buried him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	6	And now the Lord surely will render you mercy and truth, and I also will, requite you for this good turn, because you have done this thing.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	7	Let your hands be strengthened, and be ye men of valour: for although your master Saul be dead, yet the house of Juda hath anointed me to be their king.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	8	But Abner the son of Ner, general of Saul's army, took Isboseth the son of Saul, and led him about through the camp?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	9	And made him king over Galaad, and, over Gessuri, and over Jezrahel, and over Ephraim, and over Benjamin, and over all Israel.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	10	Isboseth the son of Saul was forty years old when he began to reign over, Israel, and he reigned two years: and only the house of Juda followed David.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	11	And the number of the days that David abode, reigning in Hebron over the house of Juda, was seven years and six months.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	12	And Abner the son of Ner, and the servants of Isboseth the son of Saul, went out from the camp to Gabaon.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	13	And Joab the son of Sarvia, and the servants of David went out, and met them by the pool of Gabaon. And when they were come together, they sat down over against one another: the one on the one side of the pool, and the other on the other side.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	14	And Abner said to Joab: Let the young men rise, and play before us. And Joab answered: Let them rise.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	15	Then there arose and went over twelve in number of Benjamin, of the part of Isboseth the son of Saul, and twelve of the servants of David.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	16	And every one catching his fellow, by the head, thrust his sword into the side of his adversary, and they fell down together: and the name of the place was called: The field of the valiant, in Gabaon.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	17	And there was a very fierce battle that day: and Abner was put to flight, with the men of Israel, by the servants of David.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	18	And there were the three sons of Sarvia there, Joab, and Abisai, and Asael: now Asael was a most swift runner, like one of the roes that abide in the woods.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	19	And Asael pursued after Abner, and turned not to the right hand nor to the left from following Abner.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	20	And Abner looked behind him, and said: Art thou Asael? And he answered: I am.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	21	And Abner said to him: Go to the right hand or to the left, and lay hold on one of the young men and take thee his spoils. But Asael would not leave off following him close.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	22	And again Abner said to Asael: Go off, and do not follow me, lest I be obliged to stab thee to the ground, and I shall not be able to hold up my face to Joab thy brother.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	23	But he refused to hearken to him, and would not turn aside: wherefore Abner struck him with his spear with a back stroke in the groin, and thrust him through, and he died upon the spot: and all that came to the place where Asael fell down and died stood still.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	24	Now while Joab and Abisai pursued after Abner, the sun went down: and they came as far as the hill of the aqueduct, that lieth over against the valley by the way of the wilderness in Gabaon.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	25	And the children of Benjamin gathered themselves together to Abner: and being joined in one body, they stood on the top of a hill.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	26	And Abner cried out to Joab, and said: Shall thy sword rage unto utter destruction? knowest thou not that it is dangerous to drive people to despair? how long dost thou defer to bid the people cease from pursuing after their brethren?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	27	And Joab said: As the Lord liveth, if thou hadst spoke sooner, even in the morning the people should have retired from pursuing after their brethren.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	28	Then Joab sounded the trumpet, and all the army stood still, and did not pursue after Israel any farther, nor fight any more.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	29	And Abner and his men walked all that night through the plains: and they passed the Jordan, and having gone through all Beth-horon, came to the camp.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	30	And Joab returning, after he had left Abner, assembled all the people: and there were wanting of David's servants nineteen men, beside Asael.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	2	31	But the servants of David had killed of Benjamin, and of the men that were with Abner, three hundred and sixty, who all died.
