2 Kings	2Ki	10	8	10	And Thou sent Joram his son to king David, to salute him, and to congratulate with him, and to return him thanks: because he had fought against Adarezer, and had defeated him. For Thou was an enemy to Adarezer, and in his hand were vessels of gold, and vessels of silver, and vessels of brass:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	8	11	And king David dedicated them to the Lord, together with the silver and gold that he had dedicated of all the nations, which he had subdued:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	8	12	Of Syria, and of Moab, and of the children of Ammon, and of the Philistines, and of Amalec, and of the spoils of Adarezer the son of Rohob king of Soba.
