2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	18	They passed the fords before the king, that they might help over the king's household, and do according to his commandment. And Semei the son of Gera falling down before the king, when he was come over the Jordan,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	19	Said to him: Impute not to me, my lord, the iniquity, nor remember the injuries of thy servant on the day that thou, my lord, the king, wentest out of Jerusalem, nor lay it up in thy heart, O king.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	20	For I thy servant acknowledge my sin: and therefore I am come this day the first of all the house of Joseph, and am come down to meet my lord the king.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	21	But Abisai the son of Sarvia answering, said: Shall Semei for these words not be put to death, because he cursed the Lord's anointed?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	22	And David said: What have I to do with you, ye sons of Sarvia? why are you a satan this day to me? shall there any man be killed this day in Israel? do not I know that this day I am made king over Israel?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	23	And the king said to Semei: Thou shalt not die. And he swore unto him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	24	And Miphiboseth the son of Saul came down to meet the king, and he had neither washed his feet, nor trimmed his beard: nor washed his garments from the day that the king went out, until the day of his return in peace.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	25	And when he met the king at Jerusalem, the king said to him: Why camest thou not with me, Miphiboseth?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	26	And he answering, said: My lord, O king, my servant despised me: for I thy servant spoke to him to saddle me an ass, that I might get on and go with the king: for I thy servant am lame.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	27	Moreover he hath also accused me thy servant to thee, my lord the king: but thou my lord the king art as an angel of God, do what pleaseth thee.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	28	For all of my father's house were no better than worthy of death before my lord the king; and thou hast set me thy servant among the guests of thy table: what just complaint therefore have I? or what right to cry any more to the king?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	29	Then the king said to him: Why speakest thou any more? what I have said is determined: thou and Siba divide the possessions.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	30	And Miphiboseth answered the king: Yea, let him take all, for as much as my lord the king is returned peaceably into his house.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	31	Berzellai also the Galaadite coming down from Rogelim, brought the king over the Jordan, being ready also to wait on him beyond the river.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	32	Now Berzellai the Galaadite was of a great age, that is to say, fourscore years old, and he provided the king with sustenance when he abode in the camp: for he was a man exceeding rich.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	33	And the king said to Berzellai: Come with me that thou mayest rest secure with me in Jerusalem.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	34	And Berzellai said to the king: How many are the days of the years of my life, that I should go up with the king to Jerusalem?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	35	I am this day fourscore years old, are my senses quick to discern sweet and bitter? or can meat or drink delight thy servant? or can I hear any more the voice of singing men and singing women? why should thy servant be a burden to my lord, the king?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	36	I thy servant will go on a little way from the Jordan with thee: I need not this recompense.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	37	But I beseech thee let thy servant return, and die in my own city, and be buried by the sepulchre of my father, and of my mother. But there is thy servant Chamaam, let him go with thee, my lord, the king, and do to him whatsoever seemeth good to thee.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	38	Then the king said to him: Let Chamaam go over with me, and I will do for him whatsoever shall please thee, and all that thou shalt ask of me, thou shalt obtain.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	39	And when all the people and the king had passed over the Jordan, the king kissed Berzellai, and blessed him: and he returned to his own place.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	40	So the king went on to Galgal, and Chamaam with him. Now all the people of Juda had brought the king over, and only half of the people of Israel were there.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	41	Therefore all the men of Israel running together to the king, said to him: Why have our brethren the men of Juda stolen thee away, and have brought the king and his household over the Jordan, and all the men of David with him?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	42	And all the men of Juda answered the men of Israel: Because the king is nearer to me: why art thou angry for this matter? have we eaten any thing of the king's, or have any gifts been given us?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	19	43	And the men of Israel answered the men of Juda, and said: I have ten parts in the king more than thou, and David belongeth to me more than to thee: why hast thou done me a wrong, and why was it not told me first, that I might bring back my king? And the men of Juda answered more harshly than the men of Israel.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	1	And there happened to be there a man of Belial, whose name was Seba, the son of Bochri, a man of Jemini: and he sounded the trumpet, and said: We have no part in David, nor inheritance in the son of Isai: return to thy dwellings, O Israel.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	2	And all Israel departed from David, and followed Seba the son of Bochri: but the men of Juda stuck to their king from the Jordan unto Jerusalem.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	3	And when the king was come into his house at Jerusalem, he took the ten women his concubines, whom he had left to keep the house, and put them in ward, allowing them provisions: and he went not in unto them, but they were shut up unto the day of their death living in widowhood.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	4	And the king said to Amasa: Assemble to me all the men of Juda against the third day, and be thou here present.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	5	So Amasa went to assemble the men of Juda, but he tarried beyond the set time which the king had appointed him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	6	And David said to Abisai: Now will Seba the son of Bochri do us more harm than did Absalom: take thou therefore the servants of thy lord, and pursue after him, lest he find fenced cities, and escape us.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	7	So Joab's men went out with him, and the Cerethi and the Phelethi: and all the valiant men went out of Jerusalem to pursue after Seba the son of Bochri.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	8	And when they were at the great stone which is in Gabaon, Amasa coming met them. And Joab had on a close coat of equal length with his habit, and over it was girded with a sword hanging down to his flank, in a scabbard, made in such manner as to come out with the least motion and strike.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	9	And Joab said to Amasa: God save thee, my brother. And he took Amasa by the chin with his right hand to kiss him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	10	But Amasa did not take notice of the sword, which Joab had, and he struck him in the side, and shed out his bowels to the ground, and gave him not a second wound, and he died. And Joab, and Abisai his brother pursued after Seba the son of Bochri.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	11	In the mean time some men of Joab's company stopping at the dead body of Amasa, said: Behold he that would have been in Joab's stead the companion of David.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	12	And Amasa imbrued with blood, lay in the midst of the way. A certain man saw this that all the people stood still to look upon him, so he removed Amasa out of the highway into the field, and covered him with a garment, that they who passed might not stop on his account.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	13	And when he was removed out of the way, all the people went on following Joab to pursue after Seba the son of Bochri.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	14	Now he had passed through all the tribes of Israel unto Abela and Bethmaacha: and all the chosen men were gathered together unto him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	15	And they came, and besieged him in Abela, and in Bethmaacha, and they cast up works round the city, and the city was besieged: and all the people that were with Joab, laboured to throw down the walls.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	16	And a wise woman cried out from the city: Hear, hear, and say to Joab: Come near hither, and I will speak with thee.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	17	And when he was come near to her, she said to him: Art thou Joab? And he answered: I am. And she spoke thus to him: Hear the words of thy handmaid. He answered: I do hear.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	18	And she again said: A saying was used in the old proverb: They that inquire, let them inquire in Abela: and so they made an end.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	19	Am not I she that answer truth in Israel, and thou seekest to destroy the city, and to overthrow a mother in Israel? Why wilt thou throw down the inheritance of the Lord?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	20	And Joab answering said: God forbid, God forbid that I should, I do not throw down, nor destroy.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	21	The matter is not so, but a man of mount Ephraim, Seba the son of Bochri by name, hath lifted up his hand against king David: deliver him only, and we will depart from the city. And the woman said to Joab: Behold his head shall be thrown to thee from the wall.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	22	So she went to all the people, and spoke to them wisely: and they cut off the head of Seba the son of Bochri, and cast it out to Joab. And he sounded the trumpet, and they departed from the city, every one to their home: and Joab returned to Jerusalem to the king.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	23	So Joab was over all the army of Israel: and Banaias the son of Joiada was over the Cerethites and Phelethites,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	24	But Aduram over the tributes: and Josaphat the son of Ahilud was recorder.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	25	And Siva was scribe: and Sadoc and Abiathar, priests.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	20	26	And Ira the Jairite was the priest of David.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	1	And there was a famine in the days of David for three years successively: and David consulted the oracle of the Lord. And the Lord said: It is for Saul, and his bloody house, because he slew the Gabaonites.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	2	Then the king, calling for the Gabaonites, said to them: (Now the Gabaonites were not of the children of Israel, but the remains of the Amorrhites: I and the children of Israel had sworn to them, and Saul sought to slay them out of zeal, as it were for the children of Israel and Juda:)
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	3	David therefore said to the Gabaonites: What shall I do for you? and what shall be the atonement for you, that you may bless the inheritance of the Lord?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	4	And the Gabaonites said to him: We have no contest about silver and gold, but against Saul and against his house: neither do we desire that any man be slain of Israel. And the king said to them: What will you then that I should do for you?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	5	And they said to the king: The man that crushed us and oppressed us unjustly, we must destroy in such manner that there be not so much as one left of his stock in all the coasts of Israel.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	6	Let seven men of his children be delivered unto us, that we may crucify them to the Lord in Gabaa of Saul, once the chosen of the Lord. And the king said: I will give them.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	7	And the king spared Miphiboseth the son of Jonathan the son of Saul, because of the oath of the Lord, that had been between David and Jonathan the son of Saul.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	8	So the king took the two sons of Respha the daughter of Aia, whom she bore to Saul, Armoni, and Miphiboseth: and the five sons of Michol the daughter of Saul, whom she bore to Hadriel the son of Berzellai, that was of Molathi:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	9	And gave them into the hands of the Gabaonites: and they crucified them on a hill before the Lord: and these seven died together in the first days of the harvest, when the barley began to be reaped.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	10	And Respha the daughter of Aia took haircloth, and spread it under her upon the rock from the beginning of the harvest, till water dropped upon them out of heaven: and suffered neither the birds to tear them by day, nor the beasts by night.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	11	And it was told David, what Respha the daughter of Aia, the concubine of Saul, had done.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	12	And David went, and took the bones of Saul, and the bones of Jonathan his son from the men of Jabes Galaad, who had stolen them from the street of Bethsan, where the Philistines had hanged them when they had slain Saul in Gelboe.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	13	And he brought from thence the bones of Saul, and the bones of Jonathan his son, and they gathered up the bones of them that were crucified,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	14	And they buried them with the bones of Saul, and of Jonathan his son in the land of Benjamin, in the side, in the sepulchre of Cis his father: and they did all that the king had commanded, and God shewed mercy again to the land after these things.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	15	And the Philistines made war again against Israel, and David went down, and his servants with him, and fought against the Philistines. And David growing faint,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	16	Jesbibenob, who was of the race of Arapha, the iron of whose spear weighed three hundred ounces, being girded with a new sword, attempted to kill David.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	17	And Abisai the son of Sarvia rescued him, and striking the Philistine killed him. Then David's men swore unto him, saying: Thou shalt go no more out with us to battle, lest thou put out the lamp of Israel.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	18	There was also a second battle in Gob against the Philistines: then Sobochai of Husathi slew Saph of the race of Arapha of the family of the giants.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	19	And there was a third battle in Gob against the Philistines, in which Adeodatus the son of the Forrest an embroiderer of Bethlehem slew Goliath the Gethite, the shaft of whose spear was like a weaver's beam.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	20	A fourth battle was in Geth. where there was a man of great stature, that had six fingers on each hand, and six toes on each foot, four and twenty in all, and he was of the race of Arapha.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	21	And he reproached Israel: and Jonathan the son of Samae the brother of David slew him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	21	22	These four were born of Arapha in Geth, and they fell by the hand of David, and of his servants.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	1	And David spoke to the Lord the words of this canticle, in the day that the Lord delivered him out of the hand of all his enemies, and out of the hand of Saul,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	2	And he said: The Lord is my rock, and my strength, and my saviour.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	3	God is my strong one, in him will I trust: my shield, and the horn of my salvation: he lifteth me up, and is my refuge: my saviour, thou wilt deliver me from iniquity.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	4	I will call on the Lord who is worthy to be praised: and I shall be saved from my enemies.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	5	For the pangs of death have surrounded me: the floods of Belial have made me afraid.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	6	The cords of hell compassed me: the snares of death prevented me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	7	In my distress I will call upon the Lord, and I will cry to my God: and he will hear my voice out of his temple, and my cry shall come to his ears.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	8	The earth shook and trembled, the foundations of the mountains were moved, and shaken, because he was angry with them.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	9	A smoke went up from his nostrils, and a devouring fire out of his mouth: coals were kindled by it.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	10	He bowed the heavens, and came down: and darkness was under his feet.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	11	And he rode upon the cherubims, and flew: and slid upon the wings of the wind.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	12	He made darkness a covering round about him: dropping waters out of the clouds of the heavens.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	13	By the brightness before him, the coals of fire were kindled.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	14	The Lord shall thunder from heaven: and the most high shall give forth his voice.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	15	He shot arrows and scattered them: lightning, and consumed them.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	16	And the overflowings of the sea appeared, and the foundations of the world were laid open at the rebuke of the Lord, at the blast of the spirit of his wrath.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	17	He sent from on high, and took me, and drew me out of many waters.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	18	He delivered me from my most mighty enemy, and from them that hated me: for they were too strong for me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	19	He prevented me in the day of my affliction, and the Lord became my stay.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	20	And he brought me forth into a large place, he delivered me, because I pleased him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	21	The Lord will reward me according to my justice: and according to the cleanness of my hands he will render to me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	22	Because I have kept the ways of the Lord, and have not wickedly departed from my God.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	23	For all his judgments are in my sight: and his precepts I have not removed from me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	24	And I shall be perfect with him: and shall keep myself from my iniquity.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	25	And the Lord will recompense me according to my justice: and according to the cleanness of my hands in the sight of his eyes.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	26	With the holy one thou wilt be holy: and with the valiant perfect.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	27	With the elect thou wilt be elect: and with the perverse thou wilt be perverted.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	28	And the poor people thou wilt save: and with thy eyes thou wilt humble the haughty.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	29	For thou art my lamp, O Lord: and thou, O Lord, wilt enlighten my darkness.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	30	For in thee I will run girded: in my God I will leap over the wall.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	31	God, his way is immaculate, the word of the Lord is tried by fire: he is the shield of all that trust in him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	32	Who is God but the Lord: and who is strong but our God?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	33	God who hath girded me with strength, and made my way perfect.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	34	Making my feet like the feet of harts, and setting me upon my high places.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	35	He teacheth my bands to war: and maketh my arms like a bow of brass.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	36	Thou hast given me the shield of my salvation: and thy mildness hath multiplied me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	37	Thou shalt enlarge my steps under me: and my ankles shall not fail.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	38	I will pursue after my enemies, and crush them: and will not return again till I consume them.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	39	I will consume them and break them in pieces, so that they shall not rise: they shall fall under my feet.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	40	Thou hast girded me with strength to battle: thou hast made them that resisted me to bow under me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	41	My enemies thou hast made to turn their back to me: them that hated me, and I shall destroy them.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	42	They shall cry, and there shall be none to save: to the Lord, and he shall not hear them.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	43	I shall beat them as small as the dust of the earth: I shall crush them and spread them abroad like the mire of the streets.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	44	Thou wilt save me from the contradictions of my people: thou wilt keep me to be the head of the Gentiles: the people which I know not, shall serve me,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	45	The sons of the stranger will resist me, at the hearing of the ear they will obey me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	46	The strangers are melted away, and shall be straitened in their distresses.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	47	The Lord liveth, and my God is blessed: and the strong God of my salvation shall be exalted:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	48	God who giveth me revenge, and bringest down people under me,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	49	Who bringest me forth from my enemies, and liftest me up from them that resist me: from the wicked man thou shalt deliver me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	50	Therefore will I give thanks to thee. O Lord, among the Gentiles, and will sing to thy name.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	22	51	Giving great salvation to his king, and shewing mercy to David his anointed, and to his seed for ever.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	1	Now these are David's last words. David the son of Isai said: The man to whom it was appointed concerning the Christ of the God of Jacob, the excellent psalmist of Israel said:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	2	The spirit of the Lord hath spoken by me and his word by my tongue.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	3	The God of Israel said to me, the strong one of Israel spoke, the ruler of men, the just ruler in the fear of God.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	4	As the light of the morning, when the sun riseth, shineth in the morning without clouds, and as the grass springeth out of the earth by rain.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	5	Neither is my house so great with God, that he should make with me an eternal covenant, firm in all things and assured. For he is all my salvation, and all my will: neither is there ought thereof that springeth not up.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	6	But transgressors shall all of them be plucked up as thorns: which are not taken away with hands.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	7	And if a man will touch them, he must be armed with iron and with the staff of a lance: but they shall be set on fire and burnt to nothing.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	8	These are the names of the valiant men of David. Jesbaham sitting in the chair was the wisest chief among the three, he was like the most tender little worm of the wood, who killed eight hundred men at one onset.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	9	After him was Eleazar the son of Dodo the Ahohite, one of the three valiant men that were with David when they defied the Philistines, and they were there gathered together to battle.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	10	And when the men of Israel were gone away, he stood and smote the Philistines till his hand was weary, and grew stiff with the sword: and the Lord wrought a great victory that day: and the people that were fled away, returned to take spoils of them that were slain.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	11	And after him was Semma the son of Age of Arari. And the Philistines were gathered together in a troop: for there was a field full of lentils. And when the people were fled from the face of the Philistines,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	12	He stood in the midst of the field, and defended it, and defeated the Philistines: and the Lord gave a great victory.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	13	Moreover also before this the three who were princes among the thirty, went down and came to David in the harvest time into the cave of Odollam: and the camp of the Philistines was in the valley of the giants.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	14	And David was then in a hold. and there was a garrison of the Philistines then in Bethlehem.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	15	And David longed, and said: O that some man would get me a drink of the water out of the cistern, that is in Bethlehem, by the gate.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	16	And the three valiant men broke through the camp of the Philistines, and drew water out of the cistern of Bethlehem, that was by the gate, and brought it to David: but he would not drink, but offered it to the Lord,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	17	Saying: The Lord be merciful to me, that I may not do this: shall I drink the blood of these men that went, and the peril of their lives? therefore he would not drink. These things did these three mighty men.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	18	Abisai also the brother of Joab, the son of Sarvia, was chief among three: and he lifted up his spear against three hundred whom he slew, and he was renowned among the three,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	19	And the noblest of three, and was their chief, but to the three first he attained not.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	20	And Banaias the son of Joiada a most valiant man, of great deeds, of Cabseel: he slew the two lions of Moab, and he went down, and slew a lion in the midst of a pit, in the time of snow.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	21	He also slew an Egyptian, a man worthy to be a sight, having a spear in his hand: but he went down to him with a rod, and forced the spear out of the hand of the Egyptian, and slew him with his own spear.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	22	These things did Banaias the son of Joiada.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	23	And he was renowned among the three valiant men, who were the most honourable among the thirty: but he attained not to the first three: and David made him of his privy council.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	24	Asael the brother of Joab was one of the thirty, Elehanan the son of Dodo of Bethlehem.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	25	Semma of Harodi, Elica of Harodi,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	26	Heles of Phalti, Hira the son of Acces of Thecua,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	27	Abiezer of Anathoth, Mobonnai of Husati,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	28	Selmon the Ahohite, Maharai the Netophathite,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	29	Heled the son of Baana, also a Netophathite, Ithai the son of Ribai of Gabaath of the children of Benjamin,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	30	Banaia the Pharathonite, Heddai of the torrent Gaas,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	31	Abialbon the Arbathite, Azmaveth of Beromi,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	32	Eliaba of Salaboni. The sons of Jassen, Jonathan,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	33	Semma of Orori, Aliam the son of Sarar the Arorite,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	34	Eliphelet the son of Aasbai the son of Machati, Eliam the son of Achitophel the Gelonite,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	35	Hesrai of Carmel, Pharai of Arbi,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	36	Igaal the son of Nathan of Soba, Bonni of Gadi,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	37	Selec of Ammoni, Naharai the Berothite, armourbearer of Joab the son of Sarvia,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	38	Ira the Jethrite, Gareb also a Jethrite;
2 Kings	2Ki	10	23	39	Urias the Hethite, thirty and seven in all.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	1	And the anger of the Lord was again kindled against Israel, and stirred up David among them, saying: Go, number Israel and Juda.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	2	And the king said to Joab the general of his army: Go through all the tribes of Israel from Dan to Bersabee, and number ye the people that I may know the number of them.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	3	And Joab said to the king: The Lord thy God increase thy people, and make them as many more as they are now, and again multiply them a hundredfold in the sight of my lord the king: but what meaneth my lord the king by this kind of thing?
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	4	But the king's words prevailed over the words of Joab, and of the captains of the army: and Joab, and the captains of the soldiers went out from the presence of the king, to number the people of Israel.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	5	And when they had passed the Jordan, they came to Aroer to the right side of the city, which is in the vale of Gad.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	6	And by Jazer they passed into Galaad, and to the lower land of Hodsi, and they came into the woodlands of Dan. And going about by Sidon,
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	7	They passed near the walls of Tyre, and all the land of the Hevite, and the Chanaanite, and they came to the south of Juda into Bersabee:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	8	And having gone through the whole land, after nine months and twenty days, they came to Jerusalem.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	9	And Joab gave up the sum of the number of the people to the king, and there were found of Israel eight hundred thousand valiant men that drew the sword: and of Juda five hundred thousand fighting men.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	10	But David's heart struck him, after the people were numbered: and David said to the Lord: I have sinned very much in what I have done: but I pray thee, O Lord, to take away the iniquity of thy servant, because I have done exceeding foolishly.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	11	And David arose in the morning, and the word of the Lord came to Gad the prophet and the seer of David, saying:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	12	Go, and say to David: Thus saith the Lord: I give thee thy choice of three things, choose one of them which thou wilt, that I may do it to thee.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	13	And when Gad was come to David, he told him, saying: Either seven years of famine shall come to thee in thy land: or thou shalt flee three months before thy adversaries, and they shall pursue thee: or for three days there shall be a pestilence in thy land. Now therefore deliberate, and see what answer I shall return to him that sent me.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	14	And David said to Gad: I am in a great strait: but it is better that I should fall into the hands of the Lord (for his mercies are many) than into the hands of men.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	15	And the Lord sent a pestilence upon Israel, from the morning unto the time appointed, and there died of the people from Dan to Bersabee seventy thousand men.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	16	And when the angel of the Lord had stretched out his hand over Jerusalem to destroy it, the Lord had pity on the affliction, and said to the angel that slew the people: It is enough: now hold thy hand. And the angel of the Lord was by the threshingfloor of Areuna the Jebusite.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	17	And David said to the Lord, when he saw the angel striking the people: It is I; I am he that have sinned, I have done wickedly: these that are the sheep, what have they done? let thy hand, I beseech thee, be turned against me, and against my father's house.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	18	And Gad came to David that day, and said: Go up, and build an altar to the Lord in the threshingfloor of Areuna the Jebusite.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	19	And David went up according to the word of Gad which the Lord had commanded him.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	20	And Areuna looked, and saw the king and his servants coming towards him:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	21	An going out he worshipped the king, bowing with his face to the earth, and said: Wherefore is my lord the king come to his servant? Arid David said to him: To buy the threshingfloor of thee, and build an altar to the Lord, that the plague, which rageth among the people, may cease.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	22	And Areuna said to David: Let my lord the king take, and offer, as it seemeth good to him: thou hast here oxen for a holocaust, and the wain, and the yokes of the oxen for wood.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	23	All these things Areuna as a king gave to the king: and Areuna said to the king: The Lord thy God receive thy vow.
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	24	And the king answered him, and said: Nay, but I will buy it of thee at a price, and I will not offer to the Lord my God holocausts free cost. So David bought the floor, and the oxen, for fifty sicles of silver:
2 Kings	2Ki	10	24	25	And David built there an altar to the Lord, and offered holocausts and peace offerings: and the Lord became merciful to the land, and the plague was stayed from Israel.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	1	Now king David was old, and advanced in years: and when he was covered with clothes, he was not warm.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	2	His servants therefore said to him: Let us seek for our lord the king, a young virgin, and let her stand before the king, and cherish him, and sleep in his bosom, and warm our lord the king.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	3	So they sought a beautiful young woman in all the coasts of Israel, and they found Abisag a Sunamitess, and brought her to the king.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	4	And the damsel was exceeding beautiful, and she slept with the king: and served him, but the king did not know her.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	5	And Adonias the son of Haggith exalted himself, saying: I will be king. And he made himself chariots and horsemen, and fifty men to run before him.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	6	Neither did his father rebuke him at any time, saying: Why hast thou done this? And he also was very beautiful, the next in birth after Absalom.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	7	And he conferred with Joab the son of Sarvia, and with Abiathar the priest, who furthered Adonias's side.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	8	But Sadoc the priest, and Banaias the son of Joiada, and Nathan the prophet, and Semei, and Rei, and the strength of David's army was not with Adonias.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	9	And Adonias having slain rams and calves, and all fat cattle by the stone of Zoheleth, which was near the fountain Rogel, invited all his brethren the king's sons, and all the men of Juda, the king's servants:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	10	But Nathan the prophet, and Banaias, and all the valiant men, and Solomon his brother, he invited not.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	11	And Nathan said to Bethsabee the mother of Solomon: Hast thou not heard that Adonias the son of Haggith reigneth, and our lord David knoweth it not?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	12	Now then come, take my counsel and save thy life, and the life of thy son Solomon.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	13	Go, and get thee in to king David, and say to him: Didst not thou, my lord O king, swear to me thy handmaid, saying: Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit on my throne? why then doth Adonias reign?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	14	And while thou art yet speaking there with the king, I will come in after thee, and will fill up thy words.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	15	So Bethsabee went in to the king into the chamber: now the king was very old, and Abisag the Sunamitess ministered to him.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	16	Bethsabee bowed herself, and worshipped the king. And the king said to her: What is thy will?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	17	She answered and said: My lord, thou didst swear to thy handmaid by the Lord thy God, saying: Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit on my throne.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	18	And behold now Adonias reigneth, and thou, my lord the king, knowest nothing of it.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	19	He hath killed oxen, and all fat cattle, and many rams, and invited all the king's sons, and Abiathar the priest, and Joab the general of the army: but Solomon thy servant he invited not.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	20	And now, my lord O king, the eyes of all Israel are upon thee, that thou shouldst tell them, who shall sit on thy throne, my lord the king, after thee.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	21	Otherwise it shall come to pass, when my lord the king sleepeth with his fathers, that I and my son Solomon shall be counted offenders.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	22	As she was yet speaking with the king, Nathan the prophet came.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	23	And they told the king, saying: Nathan the prophet is here. And when he was come in before the king, and had worshipped, bowing down to the ground,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	24	Nathan said: My lord O king, hast thou said: Let Adonias reign after me, and let him sit upon my throne?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	25	Because he is gone down today, and hath killed oxen, and fatlings, and many rams, and invited all the king's sons, and the captains of the army, and Abiathar the priest: and they are eating and drinking before him, and saying: God save king Adonias:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	26	But me thy servant, and Sadoc the priest, and Banaias the son of Joiada, and Solomon thy servant he hath not invited.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	27	Is this word come out from my lord the king, and hast thou not told me thy servant who should sit on the throne of my lord the king after him?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	28	And king David answered and said: Call to me Bethsabee. And when she was come in to the king, and stood before him,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	29	The king swore and said: As the Lord liveth, who hath delivered my soul out of all distress,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	30	Even as I swore to thee by the Lord the God of Israel, saying: Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne in my stead, so will I do this day.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	31	And Bethsabee bowing with her face to the earth worshipped the king, saying: May my lord David live for ever.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	32	King David also said: Call me Sadoc the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Banaias the son of Joiada. And when they were come in before the king,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	33	He said to them: Take with you the servants of your lord, and set my son Solomon upon my mule: and bring him to Gihon.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	34	And let Sadoc the priest, and Nathan the prophet anoint him there king over Israel: and you shall sound the trumpet, and shall say: God save king Solomon.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	35	And you shall come up after him, and he shall come, and shall sit upon my throne, and he shall reign in my stead: and I will appoint him to be ruler over Israel, and over Juda.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	36	And Banaias the son of Joiada answered the king, saying: Amen: so say the Lord the God of my lord the king.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	37	As the Lord hath been with my lord the king, so be he with Solomon, and make his throne higher than the throne of my lord king David.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	38	So Sadoc the priest, and Nathan the prophet went down, and Banaias the son of Joiada, and the Cerethi, and Phelethi: and they set Solomon upon the mule of king David, and brought him to Gihon.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	39	And Sadoc the priest took a horn of oil out of the tabernacle, and anointed Solomon: and they sounded the trumpet, and all the people said: God save king Solomon.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	40	And all the multitude went up after him, and the people played with pipes, and rejoiced with a great joy, and the earth rang with the noise of their cry.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	1	41	And Adonias, and all that were invited by him, heard it, and now the feast was at an end: Joab also hearing the sound of the trumpet, said: What meaneth this noise of the city in an uproar?
