3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	1	And the kingdom was established in the hand of Solomon, and he made affinity with Pharao the king of Egypt: for he took his daughter, and brought her into the city of David, until he had made an end of building his own house, and the house of the Lord, and the wall of Jerusalem round about.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	2	But yet the people sacrificed in the high places: for there was no temple built to the name of the Lord until that day.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	3	And Solomon loved the Lord, walking in the precepts of David his father, only he sacrificed in the high places: and burnt incense.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	4	He went therefore to Gabaon, to sacrifice there: for that was the great high place: a thousand victims for holocausts did Solomon offer upon that altar in Gabaon.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	5	And the Lord appeared to Solomon in a dream by night, saying: Ask what thou wilt that I should give thee.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	6	And Solomon said: Thou hast shewn great mercy to thy servant David my father, even at, he walked before thee in truth, and justice, and an upright heart with thee: and thou hast kept thy great mercy for him, and hast given him a son to sit on his throne, as it is this day.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	7	And now, O Lord God, thou hast made thy servant king instead of David my father: and I am but a child, and know not how to go out and come in.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	8	And thy servant is in the midst of the people which thou hast chosen, an immense people, which cannot be numbered nor counted for multitude.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	9	Give therefore to thy servant an understanding heart, to judge thy people, and discern between good and evil. For who shall be able to judge this people, thy people which is so numerous?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	10	And the word was pleasing to the Lord that Solomon had asked such a thing.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	11	And the Lord said to Solomon: Because thou hast asked this thing, and hast not asked for thyself long life or riches, nor the lives of thy enemies, but hast asked for thyself wisdom to discern judgment,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	12	Behold I have done for thee according to thy words, and have given thee a wise and understanding heart, insomuch that there hath been no one like thee before thee, nor shall arise after thee.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	13	Yea and the things also which thou didst not ask, I have given thee: to wit riches and glory, as that no one hath been like thee among the kings in all days heretofore.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	14	And if thou wilt walk in my ways, and keep my precepts, and my commandments, as thy father walked, I will lengthen thy days.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	15	And Solomon awaked, and perceived that it was a dream: and when he was come to Jerusalem, he stood before the ark of the covenant of the Lord, and offered holocausts, and sacrificed victims of peace offerings, and made a great feast for all his servants.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	16	Then there came two women that were harlots, to the king, and stood before him:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	17	And one of them said: I beseech thee, my lord, I and this woman dwelt in one house, and I was delivered of a child with her in the chamber.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	18	And the third day, after that I was delivered, she also was delivered, and we were together, and no other person with us in the house, only we two.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	19	And this woman's child died in the night: for in her sleep she overlaid him.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	20	And rising in the dead time of the night, she took my child from my side, while I thy handmaid was asleep, and laid it in her bosom: and laid her dead child in my bosom.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	21	And when I rose in the morning to give my child suck, behold it was dead: but considering him more diligently when it was clear day, I found that it was not mine which I bore.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	22	And the other woman answered: It is not so as thou sayest, but thy child is dead, and mine is alive. On the contrary she said: Thou liest: for my child liveth, and thy child is dead. And in this manner they strove before the king.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	23	Then said the king: The one saith, My child is alive, and thy child is dead. And the other answereth: Nay, but thy child is dead, and mine liveth.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	24	The king therefore said: Bring me a sword. And when they had brought a sword before the king,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	25	Divide, said he, the living child in two, and give half to the one, and half to the other.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	26	But the woman whose child was alive, said to the king, (for her bowels were moved upon her child,) I beseech thee, my lord, give her the child alive, and do not kill it. But the other said: Let it be neither mine nor thine, but divide it.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	27	The king answered, and said: Give the living child to this woman, and let it not be killed, for she is the mother thereof.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	3	28	And all Israel heard the judgment which the king had judged, and they feared the king, seeing that the wisdom of God was in him to do judgment.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	1	And king Solomon reigned over all Israel:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	2	And these were the princes which he had: Azarias the son of Sadoc the priest:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	3	Elihoreph, and Ahia, the sons of Sisa, scribes: Josaphat the son of Ahilud, recorder:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	4	Banaias the son of Joiada, over the army: and Sadoc and Abiathar priests.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	5	Azarias the son of Nathan, over them that were about the king: Zabud, the son of Nathan the priest, the king's friend:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	6	And Ahisar governor of the house: and Adoniram the son of Abda over the tribute.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	7	And Solomon had twelve governors over all Israel, who provided victuals for the king and for his household: for every one provided necessaries, each man his month in the year.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	8	And these are their names: Benhur, in mount Ephraim,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	9	Bendecar, in Macces, and in Salebim, and in Bethsames, and in Elon, and in Bethanan.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	10	Benhesed in Aruboth: his was Socho, and all the land of Epher.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	11	Benabinadab, to whom belonged all Nephath-Dor, he had Tapheth the daughter of Solomon to wife.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	12	Bana the son of Ahilud, who governed Thanac and Mageddo, and all Bethsan, which is by Sarthana beneath Jezrael, from Bethsan unto Abelmehula over against Jecmaan.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	13	Bengaber in Ramoth Galaad: he had the towns of Jair the son of Manasses in Galaad, he was chief in all the country of Argob, which is in Basan, threescore great cities with walls, and brazen bolts.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	14	Abinadab the son of Addo was chief in Manaim.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	15	Achimaas in Nephtali: he also had Basemath the daughter of Solomon to wife.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	16	Baana the son of Husi, in Aser and in Baloth.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	17	Josaphat the son of Pharue, in Issachar.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	18	Semei the son of Ela in Benjamin.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	19	Gaber the son of Uri, in the land of Galaad, in the land of Sehon the king of the Amorrhites and of Og the king of Basan, over all that were in that land.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	20	Juda and Israel were innumerable, as the sand of the sea in multitude: eating and drinking, and rejoicing.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	21	And Solomon had under him all the kingdoms from the river to the land of the Philistines, even to the border of Egypt: and they brought him presents, and served him, all the days of his life.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	22	And the provision of Solomon for each day was thirty measures of fine flour, and threescore measures of meal,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	23	Ten fat oxen and twenty out of the pastures, and a hundred rams, besides venison of harts, roes, and buffles, and fatted fowls.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	24	For he had all the country which was beyond the river, from Thaphsa to Gazan, and all the kings of those countries: and he had peace on every side round about.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	25	And Juda and Israel dwelt without any fear, every one under his vine, and under his fig tree, from Dan to Bersabee, all the days of Solomon.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	26	And Solomon had forty thousand stalls of chariot horses, and twelve thousand for the saddle.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	27	And the foresaid governors of the king fed them: and they furnished the necessaries also for king Solomon's table, with great care in their time.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	28	They brought barley also and straw for the horses, and beasts, to the place where the king was, according as it was appointed them.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	29	And God gave to Solomon wisdom and understanding exceeding much, and largeness of heart as the sand that is on the sea shore.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	30	And the wisdom of Solomon surpassed the wisdom of all the Orientals, and of the Egyptians,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	31	And he was wiser than all men: wiser than Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Dorda the sons of Mahol, and he was renowned in all nations round about.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	32	Solomon also spoke three thousand parables: and his poems were a thousand and five.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	33	And he treated about trees from the cedar that is in Libanus, unto the hyssop that cometh out of the wall: and he discoursed of beasts, and of fowls, and of creeping things, and of fishes.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	4	34	And they came from all nations to hear the wisdom of Solomon, and from all the kings of the earth, who heard of his wisdom.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	1	And Hiram king of Tyre sent his servants to Solomon: for he heard that they had anointed him king in the room of his father: for Hiram had always been David's friend.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	2	And Solomon sent to Hiram, saying:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	3	Thou knowest the will of David my father, and that he could not build a house to the name of the Lord his God, because of the wars that were round about him, until the Lord put them under the soles of his feet.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	4	But now the Lord my God hath given me rest round about: and there is no adversary nor evil occurrence.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	5	Wherefore I purpose to build a temple to the name of the Lord my God, as the Lord spoke to David my father, saying: my son, whom I will set upon the throne in thy piece, he shall build a house to my name.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	6	Give orders therefore that thy servants cut me down cedar trees out of Libanus, and let my servants be with thy servants: and I will give thee the hire of thy servants whatsoever thou wilt ask, for thou knowest how there is not among my people a man that has skill to hew wood like to the Sidonians.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	7	Now when Hiram had heard the words of Solomon, he rejoiced exceedingly, and said: Blessed be the Lord God this day, who hath given to David a very wise son over this numerous people.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	8	And Hiram sent to Solomon, saying: I have heard all thou hast desired of me: and I will do all thy desire concerning cedar trees, and fir trees.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	9	My servants shall bring them down from Libanus to the sea: and I will put them together in floats in the sea, and convey them to the place, which thou shalt signify to me; and will land them there, and thou shalt receive them: and thou shalt allow me necessaries, to furnish food for my household.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	10	So Hiram gave Solomon cedar trees, and fir trees, according to all his desire.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	11	And Solomon allowed Hiram twenty thousand measures of wheat, for provision for his house, and twenty measures of the purest oil: thus gave Solomon to Hiram every year.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	12	And the Lord gave wisdom to Solomon, as he promised him: and there was peace between Hiram and Solomon, and they two made a league together.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	13	And king Solomon chose workmen out of all Israel, and the levy was of thirty thousand men.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	14	And he sent them to Libanus, ten thousand every month by turns, so that two months they were at home: and Adoniram was over this levy.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	15	And Solomon had seventy thousand to carry burdens, and eighty thousand to hew stones in the mountain:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	16	Besides the overseers who were over every work, in number three thousand, and three hundred that ruled over the people, and them that did the work.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	17	And the king commanded, that they should bring great stones, costly stones, for the foundation of the temple, and should square them:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	5	18	And the masons of Solomon, and the masons of Hiram hewed them: and the Giblians prepared timber and stones to build the house.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	1	And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Israel came out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of the reign of Solomon over Israel, in the month Zio (the same is the second month), he began to build a house to the Lord.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	2	And the house, which king Solomon built to the Lord, was threescore cubits in length, and twenty cubits in breadth, and thirty cubits in height.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	3	And there was a porch before the temple of twenty cubits in length, according to the measure of the breadth of the temple: and it was ten cubits in breadth before the face of the temple.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	4	And he made in the temple oblique windows.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	5	And upon the wall of the temple he built floors round about, in the walls of the house round about the temple and the oracle, and he made sides round about.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	6	The floor that was underneath, was five cubits in breadth, and the middle floor was six cubits in breadth, and the third door was seven cubits in breadth. And he put beams in the house round about on the outside, that they might not be fastened in the walls of the temple.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	7	And the house, when it was in building, was built of stones hewed and made ready: so that there was neither hammer nor axe nor any tool of iron heard in the house when it was in building.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	8	The door for the middle side was on the right hand of the house: and by winding stairs they went up to the middle room, and from the middle to the third.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	9	So he built the house, and finished it: and he covered the house with roofs of cedar.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	10	And he built a floor over all the house five cubits in height, and he covered the house with timber of cedar.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	11	And the word of the Lord came to Solomon, saying:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	12	This house, which thou buildest, if thou wilt walk in my statutes, and execute my judgments, and keep all my commandments, walking in them, I will fulfill my word to thee which I spoke to David thy father.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	13	And I will dwell in the midst of the children of Israel, and will not forsake my people Israel.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	14	So Solomon built the house and finished it.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	15	And he built the walls of the house on the inside, with boards of cedar, from the floor of the house to the top of the walls, and to the roots, he covered it with boards of cedar on the inside: and he covered the floor of the house with planks of fir.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	16	And he built up twenty cubits with boards of cedar at the hinder part of the temple, from the floor to the top: and made the inner house of the oracle to be the holy of holies.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	17	And the temple itself before the doors of the oracle was forty cubits long.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	18	And all the house was covered within with cedar, having the turnings, and the joints thereof artfully wrought and carvings projecting out: all was covered with boards of cedar: and no stone could be seen in the wall at all.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	19	And he made the oracle in the midst of the house, in the inner part, to set there the ark of the covenant of the Lord.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	20	Now the oracle was twenty cubits in length, and twenty cubits in breadth, and twenty cubits in height. And he covered and overlaid it with most pure gold. And the altar also he covered with cedar.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	21	And the house before the oracle he overlaid with most pure gold, and fastened on the plates with nails of gold.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	22	And there was nothing in the temple that was not covered with gold: the whole altar of the oracle he covered also with gold.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	23	And he made in the oracle two cherubims of olive tree, of ten cubits in height.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	24	One wing of the cherub was five cubits, and the other wing of the cherub was five cubits: that is, in all ten cubits, from the extremity of one wing to the extremity of the other wing.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	25	The second cherub also was ten cubits: and the measure, and the work was the same in both the cherubims:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	26	That is to say, one cherub was ten cubits high, and in like manner the other cherub.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	27	And he set the cherubims in the midst of the inner temple: and the cherubims stretched forth their wings, and the wing of the one touched one wall, and the wing of the other cherub touched the other wall: and the other wings in the midst of the temple touched one another.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	28	And he overlaid the cherubims with gold.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	29	And all the walls of the temple round about he carved with divers figures and carvings: and he made in them cherubims and palm trees, and divers representations, as it were standing out, and coming forth from the wall.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	30	And the floor of the house he also overlaid with gold within and without.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	31	And in the entrance of the oracle he made little doors of olive tree, and posts of five corners,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	32	And two doors of olive tree: and he carved upon them figures of cherubims, and figures of palm trees, and carvings very much projecting: and he overlaid them with gold: and he covered both the cherubims and the palm trees, and the other things with gold.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	33	And he made in the entrance of the temple posts of olive tree foursquare:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	34	And two doors of fir tree, one of each side: and each door was double, and so opened with folding leaves.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	35	And he carved cherubims, and palm trees, and carved work standing very much out: and he overlaid all with golden plates in square work by rule.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	36	And he built the inner court with three rows of polished stones, and one row of beams of cedar.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	37	In the fourth year was the house of the Lord founded in the month Zio:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	6	38	And in the eleventh year in the month Bul (which is the eighth month) the house was finished in all the works thereof, and in all the appurtenances thereof: and he was seven years in building it.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	1	And Solomon built his own house in thirteen years, and brought it to perfection.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	2	He built also the house of the forest of Libanus, the length of it was a hundred cubits, and the breadth fifty cubits, and the height thirty cubits: and four galleries between pillars of cedar: for he had cut cedar trees into pillars.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	3	And he covered the whole vault with boards of cedar, and it was held up with five and forty pillars. And one row had fifteen pillars,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	4	Set one against another,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	5	And looking one upon another, with equal space between the pillars, and over the pillars were square beams in all things equal.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	6	And he made a porch of pillars of fifty cubits in length, and thirty cubits in breadth: and another porch before the greater porch: and pillars, and chapiters upon the pillars.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	7	He made also the porch of the throne, wherein is the seat of judgment: and covered it with cedar wood from the floor to the top.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	8	And in the midst of the porch, was a small house where he sat in judgment, of the like work. He made also a house for the daughter of Pharao (whom Solomon had taken to wife) of the same work, as this porch,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	9	All of costly stones, which were sawed by a certain rule and measure both within and without: from the foundation to the top of the walls, and without unto the great court.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	10	And the foundations were of costly stones, great stones of ten cubits or eight cubits:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	11	And above there were costly stones, or equal measure, hewed; and, in like manner, planks of cedar:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	12	And the greater court was made round with three rows of hewed stones, and one row of planks of cedar, moreover also in the inner court of the house of the Lord, and in the porch of the house.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	13	And king Solomon sent, and brought Hiram from Tyre,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	14	The son of a widow woman of the tribe of Nephtali, whose father was a Tyrian, an artificer in brass, and full of wisdom, and understanding, and skill to work all work in brass. And when he was come to king Solomon, he wrought all his work.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	15	And he cast two pillars in brass, each pillar was eighteen cubits high: and a line of twelve cubits compassed both the pillars.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	16	He made also two chapiters of molten brass, to be set upon the tops of the pillars: the height of one chapiter was five cubits, and the height of the other chapiter was five cubits:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	17	And a kind of network, and chain work wreathed together with wonderful art. Both the chapiters of the pillars were cast: seven rows of nets were on one chapiter, and seven nets on the other chapiter.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	18	And he made the pillars, and two rows round about each network to cover the chapiters, that were upon the top, with pomegranates: and in like manner did he to the other chapiter.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	19	And the chapiters that were upon the top of the pillars, were of lily work in the porch, of four cubits.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	20	And again other chapiters in the top of the pillars above, according to the measure of the pillar over against the network: and of pomegranates there were two hundred in rows round about the other chapiter.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	21	And he set up the two pillars in the porch of the temple: and when he had set up the pillar on the right hand, he called the name thereof Jachin: in like manner he set up the second pillar, and called the name thereof Booz.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	22	And upon the tops of the pillars he made lily work: so the work of the pillars was finished.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	23	He made also a molten sea of ten cubits from brim to brim, round all about; the height of it was five cubits, and a line of thirty cubits compassed it round about.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	24	And a graven work under the brim of it compassed it, for ten cubits going about the sea: there were two rows cast of chamfered sculptures.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	25	And it stood upon twelve oxen, of which three looked towards the north, and three towards the west, and three towards the south, and three towards the east, and the sea was above upon them, and their hinder parts were all hid within.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	26	And the laver was a handbreadth thick: and the brim thereof was like the brim of a cup, or the leaf of a crisped lily: it contained two thousand bates.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	27	And he made ten bases of brass, every base was four cubits in length, and four cubits in breadth, and three cubits high.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	28	And the work itself of the bases, was intergraven: and there were gravings between the joinings.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	29	And between the little crowns and the ledges were lions, and oxen, and cherubims: and in the joinings likewise above: and under the lions and oxen, as it were bands of brass hanging down.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	30	And every base had four wheels, and axletrees of brass: and at the four sides were undersetters under the laver molten, looking one against another.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	31	The mouth also of the laver within, was in the top of the chapiter: and that which appeared without, was of one cubit all round, and together it was one cubit and a half: and in the corners of the pillars were divers engravings: and the spaces between the pillars were square, not round.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	32	And the four wheels, which were at the four corners of the base, were joined one to another under the base: the height of a wheel was a cubit and a half.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	33	And they were such wheels as are used to be made in a chariot: and their axletrees, and spokes, and strakes, and naves, were all east.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	34	And the four undersetters that were at every corner of each base, were of the base itself cast and joined together.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	35	And in the top of the base there was a round compass of half a cubit, so wrought that the laver might be set thereon, having its gravings, and divers sculptures of itself.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	36	He engraved also in those plates, which were of brass. and in the corners, cherubims, and lions, and palm trees, in likeness of a man standing, so that they seemed not to be engraven, but added round about.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	37	After this manner he made ten bases, of one casting and measure, and the like graving.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	38	He made also ten lavers of brass: one laver contained four bases, and was of four cubits: and upon every base, in all ten, he put as many lavers.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	39	And he set the ten bases, five on the right side of the temple, and five on the left: and the sea he put on the right side of the temple over against the east southward.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	40	And Hiram made caldrons, and shovels, and basins, and finished all the work of king Solomon in the temple of the Lord.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	41	The two pillars and the two cords of the chapiters, upon the chapiters of the pillars: and the two networks, to cover the two cords, that were upon the top of the pillars.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	42	And four hundred pomegranates for the two networks: two rows of pomegranates for each network, to cover the cords of the chapiters, which were upon the tops of the pillars.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	43	And the ten bases, and the ten lavers on the bases.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	44	And one sea, and twelve oxen under the sea.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	45	And the caldrons, and the shovels, and the basins. All the vessels that Hiram made for king Solomon for the house of the Lord, were of fine brass.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	46	In the plains of the Jordan did the king cast them in a clay ground, between Socoth and Sartham.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	47	And Solomon placed all the vessels: but for exceeding great multitude the brass could not be weighed.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	48	And Solomon made all the vessels for the house of the Lord: the altar of gold, and the table of gold, upon which the loaves of proposition should be set:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	49	And the golden candlesticks, five on the right hand, and five on the left, over against the oracle, of pure gold: and the flowers like lilies, and the lamps over them of gold: and golden snuffers,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	50	And pots, and fleshhooks, and bowls, and mortars, and censers, of most pure gold: and the hinges for the doors of the inner house of the holy of holies, and for the doors of the house of the temple were of gold.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	7	51	And Solomon finished all the work that he made in the house of the Lord, and brought in the things that David his father had dedicated, the silver and the gold, and the vessels, and laid them up in the treasures of the house of the Lord.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	1	Then all the ancients of Israel with the princes of the tribes, and the heads of the families of the children of Israel were assembled to king Solomon in Jerusalem: that they might carry the ark of the covenant of the Lord out of the city of David, that is, out of Sion.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	2	And all Israel assembled themselves to king Solomon on the festival day in the month of Ethanim, the same is the seventh month.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	3	And all the ancients of Israel came, and the priests took up the ark,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	4	And carried the ark of the Lord, and the tabernacle of the covenant, and all the vessels of the sanctuary, that were in the tabernacle: and the priests and the Levites carried them.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	5	And king Solomon, and all the multitude of Israel, that were assembled unto him went with him before the ark, and they sacrificed sheep and oxen that could not be counted or numbered.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	6	And the priests brought in the ark of the covenant of the Lord into its place, into the oracle of the temple, into the holy of holies under the wings of the cherubims.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	7	For the cherubims spread forth their wings over the place of the ark, and covered the ark, and the staves thereof above.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	8	And whereas the staves stood out, the ends of them were seen without in the sanctuary before the oracle, but were not seen farther out, and there they have been unto this day.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	9	Now in the ark there was nothing else but the two tables of stone, which Moses put there at Horeb, when the Lord made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of the land of Egypt.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	10	And it came to pass, when the priests were come out of the sanctuary, that a cloud filled the house of the Lord,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	11	And the priests could not stand to minister because of the cloud: for the glory of the Lord had filled the house of the Lord.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	12	Then Solomon said: The Lord said that he would dwell in a cloud.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	13	Building I have built a house for thy dwelling, to be thy most firm throne for ever.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	14	And the king turned his face, and blessed all the assembly of Israel: for all the assembly of Israel stood.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	15	And Solomon said: Blessed be the Lord the God of Israel, who spoke with his mouth to David my father, and with his own hands hath accomplished it, saying:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	16	Since the day that I brought my people Israel out of Egypt, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Israel, for a house to be built, that my name might be there: but I chose David to be over my people Israel.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	17	And David my father would have built a house to the name of the Lord the God of Israel:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	18	And the Lord said to David my father: Whereas thou hast thought in thy heart to build a house to my name, thou hast done well in having this same thing in thy mind.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	19	Nevertheless thou shalt not build me a house, but thy son, that shall come forth out of thy loins, he shall build a house to my name.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	8	20	The Lord hath performed his word which he spoke: and I stand in the room of David my father, and sit upon the throne of Israel, as the Lord promised: and have built a house to the name of the Lord the God of Israel.
